<title>MEXICO: Banco de Mexico completes secondary participation.</title>
<headline>Banco de Mexico completes secondary participation.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-06-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Banco de Mexico placed all three direct sales of paper and six repurchase agreements whereby it had sought to drain 3.780 billion pesos from the secondary market on Wednesday, dealers said.</p>
<p>The Cetes sales were assigned as follows:</p>
<p>    AMOUNT     TERM	 AVERAGE RATE</p>
<p>    150 million    358 days   22.77 pct</p>
<p>    150 million    176 days   21.79 pct</p>
<p>    150 million     85 days   21.38 pct</p>
<p>The terms and maturities of the repurchase agreements were placed as follows:</p>
<p>    500 million     41 days   21.25 pct</p>
<p>    600 million     36 days   21.55 pct</p>
<p>    600 million     29 days   21.22 pct</p>
<p>    700 million     19 days   21.50 pct</p>
<p>    750 million	5 days   22.05 pct</p>
<p>    180 million	1 days   21.99 pct</p>
<p>*Amounts in pesos</p>
<p>(( -- Mexico City newsroom +525 728-9559))</p>
